    {
      "id": "claim_ab8c421f7458451fbf3d8485c6423c19",
      "statement": "The source tree is never modified: process_image copies with shutil.copy2 to output_path and then applies rotation and RelativePath tagging only to the copied file (new_file_path). README notes 'Make sure to back up your images before processing.' Re-runs on an existing output tree get _N collision suffixes rather than overwriting existing files.",
